<title>JAPAN: Tankan shows Japan firms see spending up 7.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Tankan shows Japan firms see spending up 7.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major Japanese companies plan a 7.0 percent increase in capital investment in fiscal 1996/97, ending March 31, following a 1.2 percent rise in the previous year, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said in its November &quot;tankan&quot; short-term corporate survey released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>FORECASTS FOR CHANGES IN CAPITAL SPENDING (1996/97):</p>
<p>						 lates     prev     1995/96</p>
<p>						 forecast  forecast actual</p>
<p>    Major firms			     +7.0     +6.6     +1.2</p>
<p>    Manufacturers			   +7.2     +7.6     +7.8</p>
<p>    Non-manufacturers		     +6.9     +6.2     -1.6</p>
<p> Small firms				   +0.4     -5.6     -7.1</p>
<p>    Manufacturers			    -2.4     -6.8     -4.1</p>
<p>    Non-manufacturers			+1.6     -5.0     -8.3</p>
<p> Financial  (201 firms)		    +1.9     +7.8    -17.0</p>
<p>    Banking  (149 firms)		   +4.1     +7.3     -6.9</p>
<p>    Securities   (27 firms)	     +10.1     -1.9    -47.9</p>
<p>FORECAST CHANGES IN CORPORATE SALES (1996/97)</p>
<p>						 latest		1995/96</p>
<p>						 forecast	     actual</p>
<p> Major manufacturers			 +4.6     +3.7     +2.0</p>
<p> Major non-manufacturers		   +2.5     +2.0     +0.4</p>
<p>FORECAST CHANGES IN CURRENT PROFITS (1996/97):</p>
<p>						 latest    prev	95/96</p>
<p>						 forecast  forecast  actual</p>
<p> Major manufacturers			+14.1    +13.3     +35.8</p>
<p>(excluding oil refineries)</p>
<p> Major non-manufacturers		   +8.1    +5.3	+16.4</p>
<p>(excluding electric power and gas firms)</p>
<p>Note: The tankan covered 9,602 companies, of which 711 firms were large. Manufacturers surveyed used an average dollar/yen rate of 106.66 yen when they made sales and profit forecasts for the current fiscal year, compared with 102.23 yen in the previous survey conducted in August.</p>
